  "notes": "Southern-soul-and-blues country — a huge rasped voice over a small live trio/quartet cut with almost no production gloss. The harmony is \"the most blues-functional here: I–IV–V with I7–IV7–V7 dominant colouring, i–iv–V minor blues, and long single-chord vamps,\" so the seventh share is the highest of any guitar-band model in this section, the minor-blues family is authored, and `vamp` carries real weight. Drums are \"2&4 played loose and roomy — a small kit, low cymbal count, high velocity variance, cross-stick on the slow cuts … Fills are pattern-breaking and unquantised,\" which is a low quantize strength, a wide velocity spread and a fill grid that fires early rather than on the turnaround. The bass is quoted: \"live electric bass sitting behind the beat, playing blues root-fifth-flat-seven motion; no programmed low end anywhere\" — hence the flat-seven passing tone and no `bass808` block at all. The counter is the artist's own guitar, which the entry calls \"the co-lead voice with blues bends and long sustained notes,\" plus a fixed female harmony in thirds. Melody is \"wide range, huge dynamic swing, blues-scale with flat-3/flat-5/flat-7, extensive melisma and rasped over-singing at peaks.\" ⚠ Boundary flag: the 12/8-adjacent blues cuts belong to `country-shuffle`. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the humanize values and the counter ratio.",
